[meta]
lang: en
title: OireMark conformance tests: Headings
[/meta]

h1. Headings

Tests for Section 3 of the specification.

h2. Levels

h3. All six levels {#headings-levels}
[code om]
h1. One
h2. Two
h3. Three
h4. Four
h5. Five
h6. Six
[/code]
[code html]
<h1 id="one">One</h1>
<h2 id="two">Two</h2>
<h3 id="three">Three</h3>
<h4 id="four">Four</h4>
<h5 id="five">Five</h5>
<h6 id="six">Six</h6>
[/code]

h3. There is no level seven {#headings-no-h7}
[code om]
h7. Seven
[/code]
[code html]
<p>h7. Seven</p>
[/code]

h3. Markers are case-sensitive {#headings-case-sensitive}
[code om]
H2. Not a heading
[/code]
[code html]
<p>H2. Not a heading</p>
[/code]

h3. A space is required after the marker {#headings-missing-space}
The spec asks for a SHOULD warning here (heading-missing-space), which tests don't assert.
[code om]
h2.Title
[/code]
[code html]
<p>h2.Title</p>
[/code]

h3. A heading line ends the paragraph above it {#headings-after-paragraph}
[code om]
Some text.
h2. Heading
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Some text.</p>
<h2 id="heading">Heading</h2>
[/code]

h3. Mid-line marker is text {#headings-mid-line}
[code om]
Text with h2. inside
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Text with h2. inside</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped marker is text {#headings-escaped}
[code om]
h2\. Not a heading
[/code]
[code html]
<p>h2. Not a heading</p>
[/code]

h3. Indentation is ignored {#headings-indented}
[code om]
    h2. Indented
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="indented">Indented</h2>
[/code]

h2. Custom IDs

h3. Custom ID {#headings-custom-id}
[code om]
h2. My Section {#custom-id}
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="custom-id">My Section</h2>
[/code]

h3. Duplicate custom IDs are an error {#headings-duplicate-custom-id}
[code om]
h2. First {#same}
h2. Second {#same}
[/code]
[code error]
duplicate-id 2
[/code]

h2. Generated IDs

h3. Simple slug {#headings-slug-simple}
[code om]
h2. Hello World
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="hello-world">Hello World</h2>
[/code]

h3. Letters in any script are kept {#headings-slug-cyrillic}
[code om]
h2. Огляд проєкту
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="огляд-проєкту">Огляд проєкту</h2>
[/code]

h3. Punctuation is removed {#headings-slug-punctuation}
[code om]
h2. What's new? (2026)
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="whats-new-2026">What's new? (2026)</h2>
[/code]

h3. Hyphen runs collapse and edges are trimmed {#headings-slug-hyphens}
[code om]
h2. Before / and / after /
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="before-and-after">Before / and / after /</h2>
[/code]

h3. Empty slug falls back to "section" {#headings-slug-empty}
[code om]
h2. ???
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="section">???</h2>
[/code]

h3. Formatting markers are stripped from the slug {#headings-slug-formatting}
[code om]
h2. Introduction to *OireMark*
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="introduction-to-oiremark">Introduction to <strong>OireMark</strong></h2>
[/code]

h3. Code span text is kept in the slug {#headings-slug-code}
[code om]
h2. The `om` command
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="the-om-command">The <code>om</code> command</h2>
[/code]

h3. Link text is kept, the URL is not {#headings-slug-link}
[code om]
h2. About [OireMark]:https://example.com
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="about-oiremark">About <a href="https://example.com">OireMark</a></h2>
[/code]

h3. Duplicate generated IDs get a suffix {#headings-slug-duplicates}
[code om]
h2. Intro
h2. Intro
h2. Intro
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="intro">Intro</h2>
<h2 id="intro-2">Intro</h2>
<h2 id="intro-3">Intro</h2>
[/code]

h3. A generated ID avoids an earlier custom ID {#headings-slug-after-custom}
[code om]
h2. Setup {#intro}
h2. Intro
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="intro">Setup</h2>
<h2 id="intro-2">Intro</h2>
[/code]

h3. A later custom ID still wins {#headings-custom-reserved-first}
Custom IDs are reserved for the whole document before any ID is generated.
[code om]
h2. Intro
h2. Setup {#intro}
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="intro-2">Intro</h2>
<h2 id="intro">Setup</h2>
[/code]

h3. Generated IDs avoid footnote IDs {#headings-footnote-reserved}
[code om]
h2. Fn1
Claim[fn1].

[fn]
1. Source.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="fn1-2">Fn1</h2>
<p>Claim<sup><a href="#fn1" id="fnref1" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup>.</p>
<section class="footnotes" role="doc-endnotes">
  <ol>
    <li id="fn1">Source. <a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
  </ol>
</section>
[/code]

h3. Suffixes skip taken IDs {#headings-suffix-skips-taken}
[code om]
h2. Intro {#intro-2}
h2. Intro
h2. Intro
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="intro-2">Intro</h2>
<h2 id="intro">Intro</h2>
<h2 id="intro-3">Intro</h2>
[/code]

h3. Heading text is normalized to NFC {#headings-slug-nfc}
The input spells "й" as "и" plus a combining breve (U+0438 U+0306); the ID uses the single character U+0439.
[code om]
h2. Мій йой
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="мій-йой">Мій йой</h2>
[/code]

h3. Lowercasing ignores the locale {#headings-slug-locale-independent}
The default Unicode mapping turns "I" into "i" on every system, never the Turkish dotless "ı".
[code om]
h2. ISTANBUL
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="istanbul">ISTANBUL</h2>
[/code]

h3. Combining marks are kept {#headings-slug-combining-marks}
Devanagari vowel signs are combining marks (General Category M) and must stay in the ID.
[code om]
h2. हिन्दी
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="हिन्दी">हिन्दी</h2>
[/code]

h2. Profiles

h3. Headings are not allowed in the basic profile {#headings-profile-basic}
; profile
: basic
[code om]
Some text.

h2. Heading
[/code]
[code error]
feature-not-in-profile 3
[/code]

h3. Headings are allowed in the standard profile {#headings-profile-standard}
; profile
: standard
[code om]
h2. Heading
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="heading">Heading</h2>
[/code]
